<title>PERU: Peru's net int'l reserves rise to $9.835 billion.</title>
<headline>Peru's net int'l reserves rise to $9.835 billion.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's Central Reserve Bank said Friday its net international reserves rose to $9.835 billion by June 18, up from $9.786 billion the previous week.</p>
<p>Peru's reserves, which have recovered steadily since President Alberto Fujimori's government took power in 1990, ended last year at $8.540 billion.</p>
<p>((-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima Newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
